{
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "testrunner",
      "runtimeExecutable": "go",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "-C",
        "tools/testrunner",
        "run",
        "./cmd/testrunner"
      ],
      "port": 8799
    },
    {
      "name": "game-server",
      "runtimeExecutable": "pnpm",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "--filter",
        "@ggd/game-server",
        "dev"
      ],
      "port": 2567
    },
    {
      "name": "game-server-seam",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "PLATFORM_GAME_SHARED_SECRET=devseam",
        "pnpm",
        "--filter",
        "@ggd/game-server",
        "dev"
      ],
      "port": 2567
    },
    {
      "name": "game-server-platform",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "GGD_PLATFORM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080",
        "GGD_WHITELIST_BYPASS=1",
        "pnpm",
        "--filter",
        "@ggd/game-server",
        "dev"
      ],
      "port": 2567,
      "comment": "game-server that can actually reach a LOCAL platform (the built-in default is the k8s host `platform:8080`, which never resolves on a dev box, so combat-env/curation always fail safe). Whitelist stays bypassed so the default-empty curation list cannot filter the roster to zero."
    },
    {
      "name": "game-server-lan",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "PLATFORM_GAME_SHARED_SECRET=devseam",
        "GAME_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT=ws://172.16.0.4:2567",
        "GGD_PLATFORM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080",
        "pnpm",
        "--filter",
        "@ggd/game-server",
        "dev"
      ],
      "port": 2567,
      "comment": "LAN group playtest — friends open http://172.16.0.4:39527 . Two things the plain `game-server` config lacks and a real 2-friend match needs (proven by the beta probe): (1) PLATFORM_GAME_SHARED_SECRET=devseam matches the `platform` config's secret, so the platform's HMAC match-create is accepted instead of 401→502 game_rejected at 開始; (2) GAME_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT points match_ready at THIS host's LAN IP, because the platform flow pushes that literal string to every client verbatim and the default ws://localhost:2567 makes a friend dial their OWN box → infinite loading. Deliberately NO GGD_WHITELIST_BYPASS: once the platform serves the real 48-champ whitelist, picks must be gated by it. IP = this host's current en0 address; re-check with `ipconfig getifaddr en0` if the network changes."
    },
    {
      "name": "platform",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "DATA_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/data",
        "CONTENT_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/content",
        "REDIS_ADDR=127.0.0.1:6379",
        "PLATFORM_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080",
        "JWT_SIGNING_SECRET=devsecret",
        "PLATFORM_GAME_SHARED_SECRET=devseam",
        "GAME_SERVER_ADDR=http://127.0.0.1:2567",
        "PLATFORM_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080",
        "GGD_DEPLOY_TIER=private",
        "go",
        "-C",
        "apps/platform",
        "run",
        "./cmd/platform"
      ],
      "port": 8080
    },
    {
      "name": "platform-invite",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "DATA_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/data-invite",
        "CONTENT_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/content",
        "REDIS_ADDR=127.0.0.1:6379",
        "PLATFORM_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080",
        "JWT_SIGNING_SECRET=devsecret",
        "PLATFORM_GAME_SHARED_SECRET=devseam",
        "GAME_SERVER_ADDR=http://127.0.0.1:2567",
        "PLATFORM_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080",
        "GGD_DEPLOY_TIER=private",
        "GGD_REQUIRE_INVITE=1",
        "GGD_REGISTER_RATE_LIMIT=20",
        "go",
        "-C",
        "apps/platform",
        "run",
        "./cmd/platform"
      ],
      "port": 8080,
      "comment": "task #174: the FAMILY-BUILD posture of the same platform — registration requires an invite code minted in the admin console (邀請碼). The plain `platform` entry stays open because it binds loopback (see config.resolveRequireInvite); this entry is what the deploy actually runs. Its own DATA_DIR so exercising the gate never writes into the dev store. Add GGD_OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=1 on a real deploy to close the first-account window too."
    },
    {
      "name": "client",
      "runtimeExecutable": "pnpm",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "--filter",
        "@ggd/client",
        "dev",
        "--port",
        "39527",
        "--strictPort"
      ],
      "port": 39527
    },
    {
      "name": "admin",
      "runtimeExecutable": "pnpm",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "--filter",
        "@ggd/admin",
        "dev"
      ],
      "port": 60721
    },
    {
      "name": "game-server-mobile",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
